WEBVTT

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.760
This is Izakaya Nobu.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.490
It's an ordinary izakaya, but 
there is one extraordinary thing.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.990
<b>Nobuyuki Yazawa (32)
 Owner of the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.600
Our front door opens into 
a parallel universe!

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>Shinobu Senke (23)
 Waitress at the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Isekai Izakaya

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Japanese Food From Another World

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:33.010
<b>The Secret of Whatsontap: Part 1</b>

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.330
Oh man, this weather is killing us.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:45.780
It was the right choice to cancel 
the eel bentos during lunch.

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:49.110
Thanks to that, we had leftover eel 
so we could have Hermina-chan's

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:51.530
<b>Eva (14)
Dishwasher at Nobu.
Resident of 
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.530
favorite dish, hitsumabushi.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.300
<b>Hermina (16)
Waitress at Nobu. Berthold's wife</b>

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.310
Shh, that was a secret.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:57.130
I wonder if we'll have 
customers in the evening.

00:00:57.130 --> 00:00:58.850
We might actually get a bunch.

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:01.300
You know, the calm before 
the storm and all?

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:03.030
The storm's already here.

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:06.630
Hm? A carriage?

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:07.540
See? Here they come.

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:11.080
Welcome.

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:11.970
Welcome.

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:15.950
Still as shabby as last time, I see.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:18.320
Thank you for coming here.

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:23.960
<b>Damian (33) 
Backeshof's underling</b>

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:21.530
I brought a new guest with me today.

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:23.970
We'll have two whatsontaps.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:25.880
Right away.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.320
Ehem.

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:34.710
<b>Backeshof (58) 
Chief of the City Council</b>

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:41.150
Now, I heard that you prepare 
eel in an interesting way here.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:45.110
Backeshof-sama, the chief of the 
city council, is requesting eel.

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:46.260
Bring it out already.

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:50.750
My sincere apologies, but we haven't 
prepared any because of the storm.

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:53.350
As impertinent as ever, I see.

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:55.350
Thank you for waiting.

00:01:55.780 --> 00:01:58.850
So this is the famous whatsontap.

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:05.280
I see, this taste...

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:08.880
Damian-kun, let's do as 
you suggested and buy it.

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:11.230
Buy? Buy what?

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:15.370
Backeshof-sama is saying that 
he will buy this place.

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:16.620
Huh?

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:19.920
I don't know from which 
country you've come from,

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:23.660
but running a place in the Ancient City 
without any backing must be hard.

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:27.770
That's why the Backeshof Trading 
Company is offering its aid.

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:28.880
You get it now?

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:32.080
Of course, it wouldn't behoove 
the Backeshof trading company

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:35.020
to be associated with a 
lowly bar, so officially,

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:38.530
Damian-kun is going to be 
the owner of this place.

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:40.770
What are you going on about?!

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:43.150
You are quite lively, Fräulein.

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:47.040
I just sent my concubine 
back to her home yesterday.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:49.140
So yes, if you are interested.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:51.380
Wha? You're asking me to be your concubine?!

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:55.320
Please stop making weird 
remarks to my employees.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:58.650
I'm fine with that long-haired girl as well.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:02.280
Hermina-chan just got married!

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.560
Oh well, so be it.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:07.900
Either way, this place is going to be mine.

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:09.660
As long as there is this.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:10.930
What do you mean?

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:12.580
This here, this.

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:17.900
You people are selling 
this as ale, are you not?

00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:20.140
Is there a problem with that?

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:25.390
A huge problem. I mean this 
is not ale. This is lager.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:26.590
No doubt about it.

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:28.280
What do you mean?

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:32.190
Backeshof-sama, they are playing dumb.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:34.900
Don't pretend you don't know.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:39.350
You know very well there is a law that 
declares that lager is a prohibited item.

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:41.630
Lager is a prohibited item?

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:44.370
<b>Izakaya Nobu</b>

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.370
<b>No eel bento service today</b>

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:50.270
The lager thing is a big problem.

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:52.140
<b>Berthold (32)
 Company Commander of 
Aitheria Palace Guards aka "the Devil"</b>

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:52.150
Is it that bad?

00:03:52.140 --> 00:03:54.350
<b>Edwin (70) 
Deacon of the 
Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:55.630
Yes, lager is something the previous emperor 
put a production limitation on

00:03:55.630 --> 00:04:00.150
because he planned to make it a special 
good sold only from the imperial capital.

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:02.570
It's incredibly delicious

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:06.520
and only the imperial family
and a very select few get to drink it.

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:10.340
If you sell it without permission, 
you'll be fined a tremendous amount...

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:13.170
In the worst case scenario,
you'll get the death sentence.

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:14.640
The death sentence...

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:18.970
The only one who can rescind that 
is the previous emperor himself,

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:21.720
but there's not enough time 
to get an audience now.

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:23.410
I see.

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:26.720
Either way, we have to come up with a plan.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:29.250
Taishou, can I ask you something?

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:30.110
What is it?

00:04:30.110 --> 00:04:32.480
What's the difference between 
ale and lager anyway?

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:34.030
Oh, that.

00:04:34.030 --> 00:04:37.530
Put very simply, ale is a beer brewed 
with a warm fermentation method,

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:39.360
with a fruity and full-bodied taste.

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:42.520
Lager is beer that's processed 
at a lower temperature,

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:45.450
and its clear appearance and crisp 
flavor are it's selling points.

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:50.490
In this world beer is generally ale, 
but in Japan it's usually lager.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:53.690
Since we do get our beer from over there—

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:56.470
Yeah, it's lager.

00:04:56.850 --> 00:04:59.010
Isn't there something we can do?

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:02.510
Of course there is something. 
We can just give this place up.

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:04.290
But that's not...

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:08.880
We only opened half a year ago and 
just got to know our customers.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:12.160
I know. I don't want to do that either.

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:16.620
If this place is gone, there won't be a 
place for Eva-chan to work anymore, either.

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:17.860
<b>Growl</b>

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:19.390
H-Honey.

00:05:19.390 --> 00:05:20.970
I-I'm sorry.

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:23.870
I slipped out before lunch, so 
I haven't eaten anything yet.

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:26.750
Everyone, let's get some food!

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:29.600
We can't be hungry at a time like this!

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:30.800
We need to eat something.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:32.410
Agreed.

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:35.490
I'm actually starving, too.

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:40.420
I'm going to make onigiri, so Taishou, 
please get some side dishes ready.

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:41.580
Got it.

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:48.380
Hot.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:06.070
Oh, what are these?!

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:08.480
Could it be?!

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:12.250
<b>Octopus Wieners</b>

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:12.250
<b>Octopus-san and Crab-san.
Aren't they cute?</b>

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:12.240
The mainstay in onigiri 
side dishes, octopus wieners.

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:15.500
When you fry them after making 
incisions, they look like octopuses.

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:16.690
Cute, isn't it?

00:06:16.690 --> 00:06:18.610
I got a squid here!

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:20.820
This is a crab.

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:23.340
Hm, so dexterous.

00:06:23.640 --> 00:06:27.210
Cutting ingredients into decorative shapes 
is an essential skill for Japanese cooks.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:30.300
What is this?

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:32.310
That's an elephant.

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:34.630
Ele-wha?

00:06:34.970 --> 00:06:38.780
Taishou, you're overdoing it. 
Nobody knows that.

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:42.140
Well, it's an animal from a faraway land.

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:46.490
Shinobu-san, why is this 
wrapped in black paper?

00:06:46.490 --> 00:06:52.230
That's not paper. It's called nori, 
and it's made from dried seaweed.

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:56.540
Huh, a strange food. Let's see.

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:57.230
<b>Onigiri
 Enjoy this special Nobu rice ball, 
stuffed with fancy ingredients!</b>

00:06:56.730 --> 00:06:57.230
<b>Crunch</b>

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:01.430
Oh, this is unexpected.

00:07:01.430 --> 00:07:05.230
The softness of the rice and the crispness 
of the nori are a perfect match.

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:07.730
The saltiness is really nice, too.

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:09.500
It's stuffed with salmon.

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:11.500
I've got tuna here.

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:14.170
The sauce goes really well with the rice.

00:07:14.170 --> 00:07:18.270
Oh, that tuna was for my night ca—

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:22.090
Taishou, we got to splurge 
a bit in times like these.

00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:24.420
I guess you're right.

00:07:26.810 --> 00:07:31.470
Taishou, let's just open up 
shop for the night at least.

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:35.040
Let's do that. Now that I've 
eaten, I feel more secure.

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:39.780
I heard the rumors and came right away.

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:45.540
<b>Holger (50) 
Blacksmith Guild Meister. 
Member of the city council.</b>

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:43.650
This place was the topic at 
today's council meeting.

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:45.540
The debate did not go well.

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:48.270
To be frank, the situation is quite bad.

00:07:48.270 --> 00:07:51.840
Backeshof told us there was 
an urgent matter to discuss.

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:53.640
It hit us all out of the blue.

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:57.610
Gotthard from the water transport 
guild fiercely defended you.

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:59.440
He had a really menacing look.

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:02.300
It was funny to see how the three water 
transport guilds banded together

00:08:02.300 --> 00:08:05.380
to protect Nobu, when usually 
they're at each other's throats.

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:07.250
Those three did?

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:11.410
Yes. Lorenz also did everything 
he could to protect you guys.

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:15.470
Even then, Backeshof still 
got the upper hand.

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:18.160
It seems he had made all the 
necessary preparations beforehand.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:21.270
This place is going to be formally 
investigated by the city council.

00:08:21.590 --> 00:08:25.540
The one leading the investigation is 
going to be the tax collector, Gernot.

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:29.610
He's the type who won't let go until he's 
gnawed the last bit of meat off your bones.

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:32.200
Gernot-san?

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:37.140
Gernot-san is a regular here. 
He comes to buy our eel bento often.

00:08:37.140 --> 00:08:39.920
Maybe he'll be on our side.

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:42.160
I'm not so sure about that.

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:46.050
One doesn't get jobs directly 
from the city council so often.

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:48.930
If he does well here, it'll ensure that 
he won't have to worry about the future.

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:51.570
Not to mention, he's not so 
soft a man to go easy on you

00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:53.940
just because he's been 
here a couple of times.

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:56.340
I'm saying this for your sake.

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:58.560
If you have a place where you can hide out,

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:00.940
you should at least make the preparations.

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:04.840
Thank you for taking the time to talk to us.

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:09.090
Yes, coming here could mean trouble for you.

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:13.020
It's fine. I'm just doing what I can do.

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:18.700
Taishou, what are we going to do?

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:20.350
Should we prepare to run away?

00:09:21.210 --> 00:09:24.460
As long as we have this 
place, we should run it.

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:26.820
But we might be arrested.

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:29.100
Or customers might stop coming 
after hearing the rumors.

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:31.620
We're running a business 
in a parallel universe.

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:35.490
I always knew that there could be 
some problems at some point.

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:37.480
I'm sure you knew that as well.

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:41.350
I guess so. Maybe it was just 
going too well until now.

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:44.720
This is an izakaya, nothing 
more, nothing less.

00:09:44.720 --> 00:09:47.610
That's why we are going to do our 
jobs while we have the place.

00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:50.860
If that becomes impossible, we'll 
think about what to do next.

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:53.870
You're right. Let's do 
what we can while we can!

00:09:53.870 --> 00:09:55.870
Yes, let's do our jobs.

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:56.980
Right!

00:09:57.370 --> 00:10:01.590
<i>Since that day, the place 
was always packed.</i>

00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:04.830
<i>The rumor that Izakaya 
Nobu might go away spread,</i>

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:09.310
<i>and many customers came
before that could happen.</i>

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:13.870
<i>Being busy distracted us from our worries,</i>

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:16.960
<i>and just when we began to think that 
nothing was even going to happen...</i>

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:22.660
<i>Fate came knocking on our 
door, in the form of a letter,</i>

00:10:23.320 --> 00:10:27.730
<i>telling us that we would 
be investigated tomorrow.</i>

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:31.290
Next up, we've got Nobu Plus.

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.020
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.030
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:40.700
<b>Ikejirioohashi</b>

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:40.250
Here we are at Ikejirioohashi. 
This is the station.

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:41.010
I like this town.

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:43.060
<b>Kenichi Nagira</b>

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:45.790
The just had it in Nobu, but 
onigiri. Or rice balls.

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:48.230
Rice balls as a drinking snack though?

00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:52.380
Is there such a thing? 
There is, maybe this way.

00:10:52.740 --> 00:10:57.260
<b>Narrator
 Teiyu Ichiryusai</b>

00:10:52.770 --> 00:10:55.140
Kenichi Nagira is going to go around the bars

00:10:55.140 --> 00:10:58.840
here to find the amazing 
dishes featured in "Nobu."

00:10:57.610 --> 00:10:59.750
<b>Kenichi Nagira's search for the "Nobu" bar</b>

00:10:59.770 --> 00:11:04.970
I've come from 246, and it's 
before the convenience store.

00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:05.290
<b>Kenichi Nagira
 Born in Tokyo's Ginza. Made his debut in 1970 as a folk singer.
 Since then, he's been active as an actor, celebrity, essayist.
 Has been in multiple shows that take place in bars or Shitamachi</b>

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:05.590
Exactly.

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:13.360
<b>Ikejirioohashi 
Onigiri</b>

00:11:05.590 --> 00:11:06.140
This is an empty lot.

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:08.610
Look more closely,
to your side: that sign.

00:11:08.610 --> 00:11:09.250
Here?!

00:11:09.250 --> 00:11:10.740
I guess it's this?

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:11.850
Yeah, let's go in.

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:13.380
Yes, this place is so fancy!

00:11:13.580 --> 00:11:18.730
<b>Shunsai Oguraya</b>

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:16.790
Shunsai Oguraya is a famous 
Japanese restaurant that has even

00:11:16.790 --> 00:11:18.370
made it into the Michelin Guide.

00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:20.680
That's their signature onigiri.

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:22.930
They put in sanshou miso.

00:11:22.930 --> 00:11:25.120
Ah yes, go ahead and
 have a drink first.

00:11:25.470 --> 00:11:28.890
Once the homemade sanshou 
miso has mixed with the rice,

00:11:28.890 --> 00:11:30.540
they gently squeeze it and...

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:32.410
Oh, they're done?

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:34.670
This is our sanshou miso onigiri.

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:38.250
This is impressive, this bowl, or plate?

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:38.790
Yes.

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:40.210
It certainly makes an impact!

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:41.090
Sanshou miso?

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:45.780
<b>Oguraya
 Owner  Horiuchi Makoto-san</b>

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:41.540
Yes.

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:42.860
Huh.

00:11:42.860 --> 00:11:45.770
That's why I think it goes 
really well with this sake.

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:45.760
Goes really well.

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:49.200
Since it can stand up on its own.

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:49.840
Exactly.

00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:50.800
I agree.

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:53.360
So, how is it?!

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:54.530
This is so good.

00:11:54.530 --> 00:11:55.570
Thank you.

00:11:57.170 --> 00:11:58.250
It can be a snack.

00:11:58.250 --> 00:12:01.500
The miso and the spicy kick from 
the sanshou are a nice match.

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:04.610
I know that you can put sanshou 
miso on top of a bowl of rice,

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:06.940
but I didn't know you could 
mix it in like this, too.

00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:07.640
Right.

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:09.460
This is a nice idea.

00:12:09.460 --> 00:12:11.180
This is good.

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:13.870
You guys from Nobu, you need this.

00:12:14.220 --> 00:12:17.010
So true. I wish their 
regulars could try this.

00:12:18.430 --> 00:12:21.280
And it goes so well with sake!

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:24.510
It really accelerates the sake flow here.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:26.160
You don't need anything
 for that, do you?

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:28.420
Hey, when did you even 
order that ayu sweetfish?

00:12:28.420 --> 00:12:29.430
So I eat them from the head?

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:32.730
Yes, the ideal way is to eat 
ayu in about three bites.

00:12:33.910 --> 00:12:35.370
Do start with the head!

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:40.440
We take our time, we grill the 
ayu about 20 to 30 minutes

00:12:40.440 --> 00:12:42.140
over the charcoal grill.

00:12:42.140 --> 00:12:45.890
That makes them crispy on the 
outside, but fluffy on the inside.

00:12:45.890 --> 00:12:47.520
Such a beautiful form.

00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:49.850
The uruka. That's what it's called, right?

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:49.980
Yes.

00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:51.880
It has this really adult taste.

00:12:51.880 --> 00:12:54.100
Yes, that bitterness is cool.

00:12:53.300 --> 00:12:55.840
Kids would just say, "That's bitter!"

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:57.410
Adults are smart, so...

00:12:58.410 --> 00:12:59.150
That's bitter.

00:12:59.150 --> 00:12:59.460
Hey!

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:00.000
It is.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.850
But when you pair it with sake...

00:13:01.350 --> 00:13:02.860
This... this is good!

00:13:02.860 --> 00:13:03.710
Bravo.

00:13:03.710 --> 00:13:08.110
Sanshou and ayu go well together 
too. If you eat them together...

00:13:07.460 --> 00:13:08.580
That's pretty good!

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:09.640
Like this.

00:13:09.780 --> 00:13:14.250
Color me surprised. I'm enjoying something 
that goes perfectly with sake.

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:18.880
As far as Japanese foods go, this is 
perfect. This is how it has to be!

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:19.540
Perfect!

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:20.550
Delicious.

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:21.680
Thank you.

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:25.190
Even Nagira-san approves 
of "Shunsai Oguraya."

00:13:25.190 --> 00:13:27.410
It's a one minute walk from 
the Ikejirioohashi Station.

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:29.090
<b>Assistance: Gurunabi                                 To be continued</b>

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:30.310
It's a super fancy place that has 
onigiri that pair well with sake!

00:13:30.310 --> 00:13:31.590
You guys should come by here, too.

